lines=['# Issue 37: conservative polarity gate','','## Result and scope','','ClearScan routes a page to the existing whole-page raster baseline when the corner-based segmentation estimate has `L(ink) > L(paper)`, using the existing sRGB luminance weights (0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722). This is an uncertainty gate, not a determination that the page is inverted. True reverse print is preserved as raster too. The sidecar records both luminances and the decision. Segmentation, its masks, region planning and source positioning remain unchanged; the normal reconstruction plan is built before the route. The baseline paints the whole source raster and draws the existing text layer invisibly.','', 'The five documents were reproduced from main `9655fcc` with release `--locked`, 300 DPI, ClearScan and glyph sharing off. The gate is true for exactly historical 1–5 and receipts 4, 6–9; it is false for the other 22. Main has 65 visible glyphs on gated pages: 22 on historical 2, 36 on historical 5 and 7 on receipts 4. Those vector occurrences become invisible while their source pixels are preserved by the raster. Source-pixel ownership and the inferred paper rectangles on main are documented in [the prior glyph-mask investigation](../REPORT-glyph-mask.md) and [the main operator audit](../main-pdf-audit.json). In particular the inverted foreground selects paper/counters rather than the strokes. The gate does not fix that segmentation or the historical coverage hypothesis.','', '## Page measurements','','Luminance is on the 0–255 scale. Hashes below are SHA-256 of the decoded page content stream. Ungated pages additionally had identical raw/decoded referenced image and font streams and ToUnicode maps; full per-resource hashes are in [gate-resources.json](gate-resources.json). A document PDF hash covers object numbering and global resources; it is in the byte table. Changed-pixel counts compare main with candidate at 300 DPI; `0` for wholly byte-identical financial, mixed and forms follows from identical PDFs. SSIM is source versus candidate in PDFium, where available.','', '| Page | Paper RGB / L | Ink RGB / L | Gate | Main stream SHA-256 | Candidate stream SHA-256 | PDFium / Poppler / MuPDF changed pixels | Source SSIM |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for x in measure:
 if x['set']!='corpus':continue
 doc=x['document'];n=int(x['page_id'][1:]); k=(doc,n);r=res[k];d=[dif.get((doc,n,e),0) for e in ('pdfium','poppler','mupdf')];g=x['ink_luminance']>x['paper_luminance'];score=ss.get(k,{}).get('candidate');score='—' if score is None else f'{score:.6f}'
 lines.append(f"| {doc} {n} | {x['paper']} / {x['paper_luminance']:.2f} | {x['ink']} / {x['ink_luminance']:.2f} | {'raster' if g else 'unchanged'} | `{r['content_main_sha256']}` | `{r['content_candidate_sha256']}` | {d[0]:,} / {d[1]:,} / {d[2]:,} | {score} |")
lines += ['', '[Pixel diffs and mask hashes](gate-pixel-diffs.json); [source SSIM](gate-source-ssim.json). The large number of changed pixels on gated pages reflects replacing main’s lossy/reduced background with the source raster, not merely changing glyphs. For each gated page PDFium source SSIM is 1.0; the 24 gated control pages have zero differing source-render pixels in PDFium.','', '## Glyph review material','','[The 65-entry glyph index](gate-glyph-panel-index.json) gives each source / main / candidate crop, 4× nearest-neighbour crop, numbered sheet row, and sheet SHA-256. The sheets are in `qualification/acr06/local/ink37/gate37/glyph-panels/`. Their known page counts are 22, 36 and 7. No ungated glyph changed: their decoded content, referenced resources and rendered pixels on receipts match; wholly ungated documents are byte-identical. These panels are material for Claude’s independent review; no independent review is claimed here.','', '## Text and search','','On all historical and receipts pages PDFium and Poppler extracted exactly the same text as main; PDFium word-search hit lists are identical for every distinct extracted word ([text comparison](baseline-semantics-probe.json), [receipts](baseline-receipts-semantics-probe.json), [search](baseline-search-probe.json)). Poppler text is identical byte for byte, so searches over that extracted text are unchanged.','', 'Comparison against hOCR shows pre-existing extraction limitations, not a route-induced change. In particular receipts page 7 has four supplied OCR words with zero-width character boxes: PDFium extracts none on both main and candidate, while Poppler does not recover them as four words. Receipts page 6 has a PDFium word-boundary merge. Poppler has additional historical word-boundary joins. [The hOCR comparison](ocr-probe.json) records these differences. Thus the stronger requirement that every OCR word be independently extractable was already unmet on main; the gate introduces no measured loss, but this result must not be described as complete OCR-word preservation. Fixing the pre-existing zero-width boxes would change OCR/text placement and is outside this route.','', '## Controls and conservative cost','','The original seed-370611 set, supplemental controls, reverse-panel and positive variants, and contextual dark-table set are listed below. Expected decisions match the luminance predicate. Every gated control had zero changed pixels against its input PDF rendered in PDFium at 300 DPI. The positive reverse-page variants emitted no vectors on main. The reverse-panel control is not gated; therefore the gate does not resolve mixed-polarity panels. The new normal black-border control is frozen by [its generator and truth hashes](black-border-new-truth.json): main emitted zero visible vectors, so this particular case demonstrates no additional vector-coverage loss. The contextual dark-table control page 3 has seven visible vectors on main and is gated; those vectors are replaced by the source raster. The 65 real-page glyphs likewise lose vector coverage, intentionally, to preserve source pixels.','', '| Set / control | Page | Paper L | Ink L | Gate | Gated pixels differing from source |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|']
for c in controls:lines.append(f"| {c['group']} / {c['input']} | {c['page']} | {c['paper_luminance']:.2f} | {c['ink_luminance']:.2f} | {'raster' if c['gate'] else 'unchanged'} | {c.get('source_render_changed_pixels','—')} |")
