lines += ['', 'Donors are deliberately retained, preserving the existing sibling-page dictionary and font inputs. Inverted-page donor masks can contain paper regions, so retaining them is a limitation rather than an endorsement of their geometry. The five ungated receipts pages have byte-identical content and referenced image/font/ToUnicode streams; no glyph panels beyond the 65 are needed. The glyph-sharing snapshot can still see gated-page observations. On receipts, the opt-in sharing run produced byte-identical output to sharing off for both main and candidate, and selected no members; this is not a proof for arbitrary documents. Document auto-selection can respond to the new size; it was not the specified corpus mode.','', '## Checks and history','','- Release `cargo build --release --locked -p scanweave-cli`: passed.','- `cargo test --workspace --locked`: passed on the final code; the first attempt failed because the legacy report shim needed the added fields, then the reruns passed.','- CI clippy and the Python CI gate suite: passed on the audited build; final run logs are under `local/ink37/gate37/`. The temporary `.venv` link was removed.','- qpdf checked 41 candidate/control PDFs successfully; OTS passed 27 distinct font programs: [machine-readable checks](gate-pdf-checks.json).','- The rejected page-wide polarity/raster prototype and glyph-colour proposal, and the failed OCR-box discriminator, remain documented in [the preceding report](prior-glyph-mask-report.md) and [polarity measurements](measurements.json). The OCR-box median could not separate normal forms 1 from inverted historical 4.','', '## Limitations','','The 300-DPI corpus qualification uses glyph sharing off. The reverse-panel control shows that light-on-dark regions embedded in a light page can escape this page gate. The gate deliberately gives up vectors for genuine reverse pages, and source-raster output increases size. Segmentation estimates are not corrected, and the existing donor inputs remain eligible; broader sharing and auto-selection combinations require their own qualification. Existing OCR geometry limitations are described above. The panels have not been independently reviewed by Claude in this engineering session.']
(E/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
